Virtio-net bringup (x86_64)
============================

One-shot probe + init helper, kicked off from `kernel_main`
before RS starts. Logs the MAC (or a fail-code) to the serial
console, same shape as the aarch64 equivalent in
`board/virt/hello.lsysl`.

Lives in `oskit.drivers.virtio` — the bringup is a thin helper
that *uses* virtio_net, so it belongs with the virtio driver
(arch-code depending on drivers is the wrong direction and
creates an import cycle with `virtio_transport_pci.lsysl`).
x86-specific only because it talks to the COM1 UART via
`oskit.arch.x86_64.uart_puts`.

    module oskit.drivers.virtio

    import oskit.arch.x86_64.{uart_puts, uart_putc, pci_read8, virtio_irq_wire}
    import oskit.kernel.virtio_pci_info_set


Render `v` as two hex nibbles (no 0x prefix) to the UART.

    vb_put_byte_hex(v: int)
        val hi = (v >> 4) & 0xF
        val lo = v & 0xF
        if hi < 10
            uart_putc(int('0') + hi)
        else
            uart_putc(int('a') + hi - 10)
        if lo < 10
            uart_putc(int('0') + lo)
        else
            uart_putc(int('a') + lo - 10)


One-nibble renderer for the fail-code.

    vb_put_nibble(v: int)
        if v < 10
            uart_putc(int('0') + v)
        else
            uart_putc(int('a') + v - 10)


Probe virtio-net and cache the BAR/cap addresses in the kernel
so the nic server (boot module) can fetch them via
`svc_virtio_pci_info` and `v_attach_pci(...)` without ring-0 PCI
config-space access of its own.

Does NOT init the device — that happens in the nic server's own
address space, so the server's copy of the transport module-level
vars (`vpci_common`, `vpci_notify`, …) is the one that drives the
ring programming. Running `virtio_net_init` here would leave the
device in DRIVER_OK under the kernel's vpci_* state, and the
server would then re-init on top, tearing down the first bring-up.

Logs a one-line MAC-agnostic probe result. `virtio_net_last_fail`
remains reserved for the server-side init failure.

    virtio_net_bringup()
        if v_find(VIRTIO_DEV_NET) == 0
            uart_puts("virtio-net: probe failed (no device)\n")
            return
        virtio_pci_info_set(
            vpci_common, vpci_notify, vpci_notify_mult,
            vpci_isr, vpci_device)
        val irq_line = pci_read8(vpci_bdf, 0x3C) & 0xff
        virtio_irq_wire(irq_line)
        uart_puts("virtio-net: probe ok (caps cached, IRQ=")
        vb_put_byte_hex(irq_line)
        uart_puts(")\n")
